cells:
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "now hum we are at the level \r

      we do data cleaning in sql just like we do in python and pandas         \r

      we do EDA in sql"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "question: sql ma eda kyu karna ha jab hamra paas pandas ha\r

      answer : their are are two reasons          \r

      - jo first level of data exploration chaya vo aap sida database ma hi kar
      deta ha fir baad ma data wareshouse banta ha fir data science team ko
      provide kiya jata ha lakin first level kuch bhi karna ka liya  databases
      ka sath directly cheeza karta ho       \r

      deko asa ho sakta ha ki data warehouse nahi banaya jo karna ha yahi karna
      ha directly database ma tho \r

      apko data cleaning and data anlysis ana chaya sql ma"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "two reasons\r

      1. data primalrily databases ka andr rahta ha\r

      2. sql is comfartable with large amount of data"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "today we learn about strings in sql "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: why because then we learn how to do data cleaning on the laptop dataset .
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "# Wildcard\r

      aap equal to operator ki jaga pattern-mathcing bhi use kar sakta ho
      strings ka andr"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "exactly match ki jaga aap pattern match bhi kar sakta ho. "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: ""
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT *\r

      FROM sql_cx_live.movies\r

      LIMIT 10"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Q: muja vo movies ka name chaya jisma sirf 5 characters ha "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT  name\r

      FROM sql_cx_live.movies\r

      WHERE name LIKE '_____'\r

      -- ya par underscore reprsent characters\r

      -- number of charters = length of charcters\r

      -- 5 underscore = 5 characters "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Q: muja vo movies nika; kar do jisma name A sa start hota ha and 5
      charcters"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT  name\r

      FROM sql_cx_live.movies\r

      WHERE name LIKE 'A____'"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Q: huma vo movies chaya jin ma 'man' word ata ha tho huma vo movies mil
      jayagi superman,batman,spiderman"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT  name\r

      FROM movies\r

      WHERE name LIKE '%man%'"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- movies ka starting ma men hona chaya\r

      SELECT  name\r

      FROM movies\r

      WHERE name LIKE 'man%'"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- movies ka end ma men hona chaya \r

      SELECT  name\r

      FROM movies\r

      WHERE name LIKE '%man'"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "## String functions\r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### upper/lower\r

      upper = sara character ko uppercase karega          \r

      lower  = sara character ko lowercase karega\r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT name,UPPER(name), LOWER(name)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### concat & concat_ws\r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "hamko har movie aor uska director ka name sath ma likhna ha     \r

      example apka data ma first name and last name 2 alag column ha huma unko
      merge karka single column bana na ha ek sath likna ha "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT CONCAT(name, ' ',director,' ',star)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: this is like python the join function
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT CONCAT_WS('---',name ,director,star)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- aap koi bhi character daal sakta ha \r

      SELECT CONCAT_WS('@',name ,director,star)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### substr \r

      and substring are same function"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- Q: extract first 5 characters from every movie"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- deko sql ma 1 sa start hota ha instead of 0 in python\r

      -- it likes range function \r

      -- SUBSTR(string, position, length)\r

      SELECT SUBSTR(name,1,5)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- its like start to end at the default final position\r

      SELECT SUBSTR(name,1)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- last characters \r

      SELECT SUBSTR(name,-1)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- last  5characters \r

      SELECT SUBSTR(name,-5)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### replace\r\nreplace the words"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- example\r

      SELECT REPLACE('Hello world','world','India')"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- replace man word ko pursha\r

      SELECT name, REPLACE(name,'man','pursha')\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: ""
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### reverse\r

      reverse karta ha apki string ko \r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT REVERSE('hello')
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "question : apka data ma kitna words palindrome ha       \r

      palindrome = sida pado ya ulta pado dono tarf sa same read hoga"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT name \r

      FROM movies\r

      WHERE name = REVERSE(name)"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### char_length vs length\r

      ya dono alag function ha \r

      where both are not same -\r

      The main difference between CHAR_LENGTH and LENGTH is that \r

      CHAR_LENGTH returns the length of a string in characters, while \r

      LENGTH returns the length of a string in bytes. This difference is \r

      important when dealing with multi-byte character sets, such as UTF-8, \r

      where a single character may be represented by multiple bytes.\r

      Example -café"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "char_length apko technically character length bata raha ha lakin lenght
      apko bata raha ha length bytes ma "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT name, LENGTH(name)\r

      FROM movies\r

      -- length white spaces ko count karka "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT name, LENGTH(name) ,CHAR_LENGTH(name)\r

      FROM movies\r

      -- dono tho same hi lag raha ha "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- vo movies deko jaha length and char length brabar nahi ha\r

      SELECT name, LENGTH(name) ,CHAR_LENGTH(name)\r

      FROM movies\r

      WHERE LENGTH(name) != CHAR_LENGTH(name)"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "observe pattern ki en movies ka name ma koi na koi special character
      ha\r

      ascent character ma farak aa raha ha  "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### Insert\r

      ek particular string ma aap koi character insert kar sakta ho kisi
      position par       \r

      iska andr 4 parameter hota ha \r

      insert(str, pos, len newstr)\r

      - str: The original string to insert into.•\r

      - pos: The position at which to insert the new substring. The first \r

      position is 1.\r

      \r

      - len: The number of characters to replace.•\r

      - newstr: The new substring to inser"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT INSERT('hello world',7,5,'india')
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### left and right\r

      left sa aap starting ma sa nikal sakta ho           \r

      right sa aap last ma sa nikal sakta ho\r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- har movie sa first 3 character chaya\r

      SELECT name,LEFT(name,3)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT name,RIGHT(name,3)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### repeat\r

      number of times us cheez ko repeat kar dega"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- example har movie ko 3 bar likna ha\r

      SELECT REPEAT(name,3)\r

      FROM movies"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### trim\r

      - [ltrim and rtrim]\r

      -  leading and trailing spcases of remove karta ha "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT TRIM('  focus        ')
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "SELECT TRIM(BOTH '.' FROM \"...............name...........\")\r

      -- dono tarf sa remove ho jayega"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT TRIM(LEADING '.' FROM "...............name...........")
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT TRIM(TRAILING'.' FROM "...............name...........")
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: deko aap aga sa hata sakta ho picha sa hata sakta ho lakin bich sa hata
      nahi sakta
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT LENGTH(LTRIM('        hello'))
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT LENGTH(RTRIM('hello         '))
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### substring_index\r

      isko aap compare kar sakta ho python ka (Split) function sa\r

      kisi ek particular character ka basis par vo string ko break(thod) alag
      kar deta ha"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT SUBSTRING_INDEX('www.google.com', '.', 2);
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: ""
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### strcmp\r

      string comparison function\r

      The STRCMP() function returns an integer that indicates the \r

      relationship between the two strings:           \r

      and comparion ho raha ha alpahatecally\r

      - If str1 is less than str2, the function returns a negative integer.\r

      - If str1 is greater than str2, the function returns a positive \r

      integer.\r

      \r

      - If str1 is equal to str2, the function returns 0\r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT STRCMP('DELHI','MUMBAI')
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT STRCMP('DELHI','DELHI')
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### locate\r

      ek given string ma kisi substring ka index postion postion \r

      (\"world\", \"hello world\")\r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- aap kis bhi character ka postion in string\r

      -- example hello world ma w ki position \r

      SELECT LOCATE('w','hellow world')"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### lpad and rpad \r

      padding ka matlab ha hamra pass kisi ka phone number . huma phone number
      ka aga country add karna ha \r

      \r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: SELECT LPAD('888888888',12,'+91')
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 2
    languageId: sql
    value: "-- isi ka similar hota r pad\r

      SELECT RPAD('888888888',12,'+91')"
    metadata: {}
